/* Solar return planet readings (each planet by house, Mercury, Venus and Mars by sign, retrograde this year) and out-of-bounds planets in your birth chart, written about you (see CLAUDE.md). */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.srPlanets = {
  "house": {
    "mercury": {
      "1": "Your mind sits right at the front of the year ahead, with Mercury in the 1st house of your return chart. People notice how you talk: quicker, sharper, more willing to say the thing out loud instead of rehearsing it in your head afterwards. You introduce yourself more often, explain yourself more readily, and find that one clever line opens doors a polished CV never did. Restlessness comes with the package, so you fidget through anything slow, lose focus mid-sentence and start three plans at once. Nervous energy shows in your body as shallow breathing on busy days or a jaw clenched without your noticing. By your next birthday your voice has become part of how people picture you, and you are known as someone with something to say.",
      "2": "Money occupies your thoughts this year, and Mercury in the 2nd house of your return makes you far more alert to what things cost and what your time is worth. You compare prices constantly, check your balance often, and price up an idea before you have finished having it. Talking, writing, teaching or selling becomes a steady source of income in the next twelve months, even if only as a side stream that grows steadily. Contracts, invoices and small print cross your desk more often, and reading them properly pays for itself. Trouble starts when a busy mind mistakes worrying about money for managing it, and you lie awake doing sums. Once the figures live on paper rather than circling in your head, your financial decisions become some of the sharpest you have made.",
      "3": "Mercury is at home in the 3rd house of your return chart, and the year ahead fills up with messages, errands and conversations. Messages keep coming from every direction, and you are always the one who knows the latest local news and exactly who said what to whom. Short trips pile up, and you are rarely in one place for long. Learning comes easily, so a new course or a regular learning habit sticks this time. Scatter is the price, with too many threads open at once and a to-do list that never quite shrinks. The people you chat with casually, close to home or in the wider family, turn out to matter more than the formal contacts you chase.",
      "4": "With Mercury in the 4th house of your return, a great deal of your thinking this year happens at home and about home. You spend time imagining changes to where you live, planning improvements or talking with family about how things were when you were small. Family news reaches you first, and relatives turn to you to sort out the practical arrangements. Working or thinking at home suits your concentration surprisingly well. The strain arrives as a noisy household, with repairs, visitors and family debates that never quite end. Sorting the practical details of where you live gives your mind a quieter place to rest, and several of your clearest decisions this year are made in your own space.",
      "5": "Mercury in the 5th house of your return chart makes the year ahead playful and talkative. You flirt with more wit than usual, create for the fun of it and return to pastimes you had set aside for years. If you have children, you spend more time talking, learning and laughing with them. Flirting turns into a word game, and whoever keeps up with your banter wins your attention fast. Romance can become a performance, all sparkling messages and very little showing up in person, and you notice when that happens to you. When your ideas turn into things you actually finish, this becomes one of your most creatively productive stretches in years.",
      "6": "Your mind turns to the daily grind this year, and Mercury in the 6th house of your return makes you the chief organiser of your own routines. You rethink how you organise your days and notice exactly where work keeps getting held up. Work brings more messages, reports and small tasks than usual, and you handle them well until you find yourself still working long after you should have stopped. Your body reacts quickly to worry, so a knotted stomach or broken sleep tells you the workload has tipped over. Health research grabs you, and you want to understand exactly how your body works and what helps it. Small daily improvements stack up until your ordinary days run far more smoothly than they did at your last birthday.",
      "7": "Conversations with one other person shape the year ahead, with Mercury in the 7th house of your return chart. A partner, a business associate or a close friend becomes your main sounding board, and you talk things through at length. Negotiations and agreements come up, from a lease to a collaboration to a frank talk about where a relationship is going. You hear your own ideas more clearly when someone reflects them back. Less helpful is the endless discussion, the same argument replayed in different words while nothing gets decided. What this year teaches you is that saying what you mean, plainly and early, does more for a relationship than any amount of hinting.",
      "8": "Your thinking goes deep this year, with Mercury in the 8th house of your return. You dig into psychology, uncover hidden history or look properly at the debts and shared finances you usually avoid facing. Conversations turn intimate, and someone close tells you something they have never said aloud before. You spot quickly when a person is holding back, and you want the whole story rather than the tidy version. Obsessive thinking is the cost: replaying a painful exchange for days, or digging into things that hurt more once uncovered. Clear, honest talks about money, trust and loss bring relief across these twelve months, leaving you far more in control of what used to frighten you.",
      "9": "Mercury in the 9th house of your return chart sends your mind travelling this year. You book a trip abroad, sign up for a course, or fall down a rabbit hole of history, philosophy or a faith you knew little about. Conversations with people from other countries and backgrounds stretch your thinking, and you find yourself quoting ideas that changed your view. Writing, publishing, teaching or anything that reaches a wider audience moves easily for you. You can get so sure of your new views that you lecture friends and miss the glazed looks. One idea picked up now keeps shaping your choices for years, which makes this a pivotal year for your outlook.",
      "10": "Your words reach the professional world this year, with Mercury in the 10th house of your return. Presentations, interviews, reports and important emails carry more weight in your career, and people above you notice how well you explain things. You end up drafting the proposal, running the team meeting or speaking for your department when it counts. Reputation now rests on how you communicate, so a clear message travels far and a careless comment reaches the wrong ears. Pressure shows as rewriting a short message five times before you dare to send it. When you trust your voice, the next twelve months bring public recognition for your thinking, often from someone you did not realise was paying attention.",
      "11": "Networks, groups and new acquaintances fill this year, with Mercury in the 11th house of your return chart. You join new groups and communities, and you come to know people in fields you had never touched. Friends pass you ideas, contacts and job links, and you pass them on just as generously. Your hopes for the future sharpen as you talk them through with people who think the same way. Overload is the snag: endless messages, group decisions that drag on, friendships kept alive only at a distance. Somewhere in all that chatter, a single conversation points you towards a goal that excites you, and you spend the rest of the year moving towards it.",
      "12": "Much of your thinking this year happens quietly and privately, with Mercury in the 12th house of your return. You keep more to yourself, speak less in company, and have your best ideas in quiet, unguarded moments. Dreams turn vivid and memorable, and old worries surface for no obvious reason at the most ordinary moments. Research, solitary writing or behind the scenes work suits you better than the spotlight. Anxiety tends to run quietly in the background, and replaying a conversation you cannot change becomes a familiar habit. Real silence turns that worry into insight, so that by the time your next birthday comes round you understand your own patterns far better."
    },
    "venus": {
      "1": "Venus sits in the 1st house of your return chart, and this year you feel more attractive, more at ease and more willing to be seen. People respond to you more warmly, compliments come more easily, and you finally invest in the look you have wanted for ages. Charm comes without effort, and awkward conversations land softly. Love and friendship move towards you rather than needing to be chased. You lean on being liked, though, and say yes to keep things pleasant when you mean no. Feeling good in your own skin becomes the ground everything else stands on, a confidence that outlasts the year itself.",
      "2": "Money and pleasure sit close together this year, with Venus in the 2nd house of your return. Income tends to improve through a pay rise, a creative side project or a stroke of luck that turns out to be worth more than you expected. You notice quality now, and you would rather own one thing that lasts than several that do not. Your sense of your own worth grows, and you ask for better terms without the usual apology attached. Impulse buys dressed up as self-care are the weak spot, and some months the account empties well before payday. Valuing yourself properly shows up very literally in the next twelve months, in what you earn, what you keep and what you refuse to accept.",
      "3": "Your words carry warmth this year, with Venus in the 3rd house of your return chart. Your words come out kinder and funnier, and a few well chosen words smooth over a family tension that had lasted months. Relationships with siblings, cousins and neighbours improve, and the small routines of your everyday life become a reliable joy. Learning appeals most when it feels creative, and you are drawn to ideas and words that sound beautiful to you. Flirtation starts easily, often through light conversation in the course of an ordinary day. You put off a necessary hard conversation because you prefer everything to stay pleasant, and it waits for you. Even so, the ordinary moments of your days feel noticeably sweeter than they have for a while.",
      "4": "Making home beautiful and peaceful takes up your attention this year, with Venus in the 4th house of your return. You make your space more beautiful, change how it feels to live there, or move somewhere that feels truly yours. Family relationships soften, and a parent or relative becomes easier company than they used to be. Sharing your home with people you love and simply resting in your own space become your favourite pleasures. Staying in wins every single time, and you notice invitations piling up unanswered. Home turns into a sanctuary in the year ahead, the place where family life feels like happiness rather than obligation.",
      "5": "With Venus in the 5th house of your return chart, the year ahead is built for romance, fun and creative joy. Dating comes easily, a crush turns into something real, or a long relationship gets its sparkle back through time spent simply enjoying each other. Anything creative or playful gives you pleasure, and you love showing people what you have made. Time with children, yours or someone else's, is particularly sweet. Being chosen thrills you, sometimes more than the person doing the choosing, and that can lead you towards the wrong admirer. Happiness shows on you so plainly this year that good people are drawn towards it.",
      "6": "Pleasure slips into the ordinary routine this year, with Venus in the 6th house of your return. Your workplace grows friendlier, a colleague becomes a friend, and you finally make the place where you work somewhere you enjoy being. Looking after your body feels like a treat rather than a chore, and gentle, pleasant habits come to you without effort. Work involving beauty, care or helping people feels particularly satisfying. Indulgence creeps in unnoticed, and small treats become daily habits while good intentions quietly lapse. Small, lovely changes to how you spend your hours make your days far more pleasant than they were at your last birthday.",
      "7": "Relationships are the centre of the year ahead, with Venus in the 7th house of your return chart. A partnership deepens, a new romance begins, or you meet someone who feels like an equal rather than a project. Business partnerships go well too, with fair deals and negotiations that stay friendly on both sides. You find yourself more willing to compromise and more openly grateful for the people who stand beside you. Your own preferences can disappear, and you go along with plans you did not want because keeping the peace is easier. What a balanced, loving partnership feels like from the inside is knowledge you carry long after the year ends.",
      "8": "Love turns intense and money becomes shared this year, with Venus in the 8th house of your return. You want closeness that goes past polite affection into trust, the kind where you let someone see both your finances and your fears. Joint finances often improve through a partner's income, an inheritance, a well timed loan or a generous gift. People with depth and a little mystery attract you far more than easy charm does. Jealousy stirs, along with a feeling that love must be proven through total commitment. These twelve months leave you braver about letting people close and more honest about what you need from them.",
      "9": "Pleasure is found far from home this year, with Venus in the 9th house of your return chart. Distant places, other cultures and unfamiliar ideas light up your year, and you fall for somewhere or something new with surprising ease. Romance can arrive through travel, study or someone from a very different background. Learning in beautiful settings delights you, and art, philosophy or spiritual ideas give your life extra meaning. Idealising somewhere else can leave you restless with the life you have. Coming home, you carry a wider, lovelier picture of the world and a fresh sense of what you love.",
      "10": "Charm and good fortune come to your career this year, with Venus in the 10th house of your return. Colleagues and managers warm to you, and your reputation improves because people enjoy working alongside you. Openings in creative, beauty, hospitality or diplomatic work come your way, sometimes through someone you met socially. Your public image softens, and you are seen as approachable as well as talented. Likeability can stand in for the harder graft a promotion needs, and a sharper rival notices. One relationship formed through work turns out to be among the most valuable of your whole year.",
      "11": "Friendship becomes one of the great pleasures of this year, with Venus in the 11th house of your return chart. You spend more time with friends, find your way into a new circle, or reconnect with old ones who make you laugh until you ache. A friend introduces you to someone special, or a friendship slowly and gently turns into romance. Your hopes for the future feel achievable because people are cheering you on. Social plans multiply until your time is booked solid and you never go deep with anyone. With the right people helping your wishes along, you feel liked in a way that steadies you.",
      "12": "Love becomes a private, tender matter this year, with Venus in the 12th house of your return. Solitude feels delicious: slow hours, quiet rituals of your own and time with nobody to please. A secret crush, a hidden romance or a love that cannot be shown in public can take shape, and you keep it close. Compassion for people who are struggling runs high, and you help without wanting credit. The risk is giving too much to someone who takes and never gives back, while part of you already knows it. The love you offer yourself in these twelve months becomes the ground healthier relationships grow from afterwards."
    },
    "mars": {
      "1": "Mars in the 1st house of your return chart gives you a surge of energy and nerve for the year ahead. You walk faster, speak more bluntly and start projects without waiting for anyone's permission. Physical activity becomes essential because your body needs somewhere to put all that heat, and hard effort leaves you calmer than rest ever could. People read you as more assertive, sometimes more intimidating than you intend, and others step back when you only meant to be clear. Minor cuts, bumps and burns come from rushing, and a sharp tone sparks arguments you did not plan. By your next birthday you have proof that you can fight for what you want and win.",
      "2": "Earning more drives you this year, with Mars in the 2nd house of your return. You chase a raise, take on extra shifts, start a side business or quote the fee you deserve without flinching. Spending turns impulsive too, and a purchase that felt urgent one day looks less necessary a week later. Your self-worth ties itself closely to what you achieve financially, so a setback at work stings harder than usual. Fights over money flare, especially with anyone who owes you and keeps stalling. Extra effort converts directly into income across the months ahead, which shows you what you can earn when you push.",
      "3": "Words turn sharp and days turn busy this year, with Mars in the 3rd house of your return chart. You say what you have been holding back, argue your point and refuse to let a lazy statement pass unchallenged. Local trips multiply, you are always rushing somewhere, and impatience on the move leads to needless haste and near misses. A sibling or neighbour brings friction, and old disputes close to home flare quickly. Learning happens with intensity when something grabs you, and you master in weeks what would normally take months. Your voice grows stronger through the year, along with a far better sense of which battles are worth the breath.",
      "4": "A lot of your energy goes into home and family this year, with Mars in the 4th house of your return. You make big changes at home, or move, with a speed that surprises everyone including you. Tension at home is likely, with arguments with the people you live with about space, noise and who does what. You feel fiercely protective of your private life and bristle when anyone crosses the threshold uninvited. Work stress follows you through the front door and lands on the people closest to you. What you build in the year ahead is a home base that feels strong and properly yours, even if the process is loud.",
      "5": "Passion, competition and creative drive run through this year, with Mars in the 5th house of your return chart. Romance is exciting and direct: sudden attractions, bold first moves, chemistry you feel the instant it arrives. You throw yourself into whatever excites you with an intensity that surprises your friends. If you have children, they keep you on your feet and occasionally test your patience. Gambles tempt you, along with reckless flings and the urge to show off at the wrong moment. You rediscover what it feels like to want something wholeheartedly and chase it, and that appetite is the real gift of the year.",
      "6": "Work and health demand your energy this year, with Mars in the 6th house of your return. You power through a heavy workload, pick up tasks others avoid, and overhaul your daily routine with military efficiency. Physical activity becomes non-negotiable, and on days you go without it you feel twitchy and short tempered. Friction with colleagues builds when you feel others are not pulling their weight, and you say so. Pushing without rest shows up in your body as strain, headaches or a deep ache after a big week. Once you accept that steady effort beats heroic bursts, both your fitness and your output climb through the year.",
      "7": "Energy and sometimes conflict pour into your relationships this year, with Mars in the 7th house of your return chart. A partner pushes you, challenges you or brings out your competitive streak over something as small as who is right about a detail. Arguments flare more easily, but they also clear the air and lead to honest change. You meet someone bold and exciting, or form a partnership that drives you forward professionally. Every disagreement can start to feel like a contest you have to win. Standing your ground while keeping the relationship intact becomes a skill you own by the end of the year.",
      "8": "Intensity runs through this year, with Mars in the 8th house of your return. Desire is strong, intimacy is passionate, and shallow connection bores you within minutes. Shared money becomes either a battleground or a project: a fight over bills, a determined push to clear a debt, or a joint investment you research obsessively. You face fears head on and deal with the news, the problem or the conversation you would normally put off. Power struggles and resentment can simmer for weeks behind a polite face. Courage transforms something that has felt stuck for years, and the lightness once it moves is unmistakable.",
      "9": "Adventure and conviction fill this year, with Mars in the 9th house of your return chart. You plan an ambitious trip, start a demanding course, or throw yourself into a cause you believe in with total commitment. Your opinions are strong and you defend them passionately, sometimes more loudly than the moment needs. Legal matters, publishing or anything aimed at a wider audience moves quickly once you push. Certainty can turn into arrogance, and you stop listening to people who have lived things you have not. Real experience tests your beliefs and hardens the ones worth keeping, and you come home with a bolder view of your own life.",
      "10": "Ambition takes centre stage this year, with Mars in the 10th house of your return. You push for promotion, launch your own business, or take a high profile role that stretches you further than you expected. Your career demands long hours, and you meet the demand with a determination colleagues notice. Clashes with bosses or authority figures are likely whenever they block your progress. Evenings and weekends get swallowed by work, and friends learn to expect a late reply. Impatience can read as aggression to the very people who control your next step. Visible, rewarded effort earns you a reputation as the person who gets things done.",
      "11": "Groups, friends and future goals absorb your energy this year, with Mars in the 11th house of your return chart. You take a leading role in a group or a shared cause, and your enthusiasm gets people moving. Friendships become more active, built around shared effort, adventures or causes rather than idle catching up. Arguments within groups break out when others move too slowly for your liking. Friends start to feel like a squad you need to manage rather than people you enjoy. Because you finally commit and act, a long term goal starts moving, pulling the people around you along in its wake.",
      "12": "Your energy works behind the scenes this year, with Mars in the 12th house of your return. You feel more tired than usual at times, and your body asks for extra sleep, rest and time alone. Anger goes underground, showing up as frustration you cannot explain or tension settling in your shoulders by evening. Quiet, solitary movement helps enormously, the kind that clears your head without an audience. Self-sabotage creeps in, and you fight yourself instead of the real problem. Private work done now, unseen and unapplauded, gives you a strong launch pad for the more visible year that follows."
    },
    "jupiter": {
      "1": "Personal growth and optimism run through this year, with Jupiter in the 1st house of your return chart. You feel more confident, more generous and more willing to say yes to experiences you would have dodged at your last birthday. Opportunities find you because people see you as lucky and capable, and you start to believe them. Travel, study or a sense of taking up more room in your own life marks the months ahead. Excess is the weak point: overdoing pleasures, spending too freely and making promises you cannot keep. Friends comment on how much you have grown long before you notice it yourself.",
      "2": "Money and resources tend to grow this year, with Jupiter in the 2nd house of your return. A raise, a new client, a well judged investment or a generous gift improves your finances, sometimes from a direction you had written off. You feel more secure and more willing to invest in yourself and in the quality of your everyday life. Your values broaden, and you care more about quality and meaning than having more. Feeling abundant makes it easy to spend as if the good times are guaranteed. Income and self-worth expand together in the year ahead, with gains that last as long as one eye stays on the outgoings.",
      "3": "Your mind and your local world both expand this year, with Jupiter in the 3rd house of your return chart. You read widely, learn fast, and have conversations that shift your perspective in a single exchange. Short trips bring luck, leading to an unexpected opening or a useful introduction. Relationships with siblings and neighbours improve, and someone close by turns out to be a staunch ally. Saying yes to every small commitment leaves you rushing between them. A piece of writing, a course or a chance remark opens a door you did not know existed.",
      "4": "Home and family bring growth this year, with Jupiter in the 4th house of your return. You move somewhere bigger, renovate, or bring more people into your household, and home starts to hold more of your life than it did. Family relationships turn warmer and more supportive, and old grudges soften with time spent together. Emotional security grows, and your front door becomes the boundary of a place you relax. Property and family obligations can swell beyond what you can comfortably carry. Across these twelve months the foundations of your life strengthen until you feel more rooted than you have in years.",
      "5": "Joy, romance and creativity light up this year, with Jupiter in the 5th house of your return chart. Your love life flourishes with dates, flirtation and evenings that run long. Creative projects succeed, and you feel inspired to create something just because it pleases you. Children bring great happiness, and for some people the year brings a pregnancy or a new arrival. Overindulgence tempts, along with big gambles taken on a lucky feeling. Play feels like a pleasure again rather than a waste of time, which lets happiness arrive more easily than it has for ages.",
      "6": "Work and health both improve this year, with Jupiter in the 6th house of your return. A better job, a promotion or more satisfying daily tasks come your way, and the working week stops feeling like a sentence. Colleagues are supportive, and a manager or teammate goes out of their way to help you. Health routines stick, and you feel more vital, sleeping better and moving more. You take on so much work that generosity turns into overload, and indulgence creeps into the working day. Daily life turns more balanced and more rewarding, with good habits formed now carrying you for years.",
      "7": "Growth arrives through other people this year, with Jupiter in the 7th house of your return chart. Marriage, a new partnership or the deepening of an existing bond is likely, and you feel supported in a way that lets you stretch. Business partnerships and contracts bring concrete benefits, and a collaborator opens doors you could not open alone. Generous, wise people cross your path and help you grow. Expecting a partner to fix everything for you puts an unfair weight on them. Through these partnerships you become a better, braver version of the person you were at your last birthday.",
      "8": "Shared resources and deep change bring benefits this year, with Jupiter in the 8th house of your return. Inheritances, investments, a partner's income or a well timed loan come through favourably, and paperwork you dreaded turns out simpler than expected. Intimacy deepens, and you trust more readily than usual. Therapy, honest conversations or deep reflection produce psychological growth. Easy credit tempts you into borrowing more than you need, and a generous mood can sign you up for commitments that outlast the good feeling. You end the year richer both in money and in emotional depth, with an old fear noticeably smaller than it was.",
      "9": "Travel, learning and expansion define this year, with Jupiter in the 9th house of your return chart. You travel abroad, go back to study, or explore a philosophy that reorganises how you see things. Your beliefs broaden, and you gain wisdom from experience rather than from books alone. Publishing, teaching or legal matters go your way. Restlessness is the flip side, along with a tendency to preach your discoveries to anyone within earshot. Horizons widen in every direction this year, so you come home with a much larger view of the world and your place in it.",
      "10": "Career success is likely this year, with Jupiter in the 10th house of your return. A promotion, public recognition or a new position comes your way, sometimes after a long wait that makes it sweeter. Your reputation grows, and people in authority back you, recommend you and open doors. Ambition feels optimistic rather than anxious, and you talk about your future plans with confidence. Overpromising is the danger, along with a touch of arrogance when success comes quickly. A new professional level is reached in the next twelve months, in full view of the people who matter.",
      "11": "Friends and groups become the engine of your growth this year, with Jupiter in the 11th house of your return chart. Your social circle widens, and friends open doors for you, pass on jobs and introduce you to the right people. Hopes and dreams you had shelved move closer to reality. You join groups that support your goals and find yourself among people who think bigger than your old crowd. Saying yes to every invitation spreads you thin. The wishes that start coming true this year owe a great deal to the people around you.",
      "12": "Spiritual growth and inner peace are highlighted this year, with Jupiter in the 12th house of your return. Time alone heals rather than isolates, and in difficult moments you feel strangely protected, as if something has your back. Stillness, reflection and quiet service to others bring rewards you did not expect. Help arrives from unexpected sources, often behind the scenes and without fanfare. Dreams carry messages, and a chance word says exactly what you needed to hear. Escapism tempts you whenever life feels hard, and it costs more than it gives. Rested, hopeful and stronger, you meet the following year ready to begin again."
    },
    "saturn": {
      "1": "Saturn sits on the front step of your year, and people read you as more serious than usual. You notice it in how people respond to you, and in the responsibilities that land on you when nobody else wants to own them. Your body asks for structure: earlier nights, steadier habits, a daily rhythm you keep. Some mornings feel heavy, as though you carry a rucksack no one else can see, and confidence arrives slowly rather than in bursts. In return you earn an authority that is yours, not borrowed from a title or a louder friend. Looking back from your next birthday, the version of you who kept asking permission feels like a stranger.",
      "2": "Money becomes a matter of plain arithmetic this year, with Saturn in the second house of your return chart. You check your balance more often, cut the costs you had stopped noticing, and weigh every purchase before you make it. Income can feel tight or slow to arrive, and a purchase you once made without thinking now needs a reason. Underneath the numbers runs a quieter question about your worth: whether you charge enough, whether you undersell what you know. The pinch is real, and it tempts you to refuse small pleasures out of fear rather than need. What these twelve months build is a foundation you trust, a savings habit or a fairer rate that outlasts the year.",
      "3": "Words carry extra weight in the year ahead. With Saturn in your third house, you weigh every word, read the small print closely, and choose what you say to the people close to you with unusual care. Learning is on the agenda, usually something demanding that asks for real discipline and proves what you know. Daily errands and routine travel feel like a grind, eating time you would rather spend elsewhere. Some conversations stall because you hold back until you are certain, and people mistake your caution for coldness. The reward for all that effort is a voice others trust. When you speak this year, people go quiet and listen.",
      "4": "Home asks for serious attention this year. Saturn in the fourth house of your return chart often means a mortgage, a move, a lease renewed on stricter terms, or a parent who needs more of your time than before. You fix what you once lived with, and sort the paperwork that has sat untouched for years. Family duty feels heavier, and some evenings your own house does not feel like a place to rest. Old patterns from childhood surface in how you react to criticism, mess or noise. Much of this work stays invisible to friends and colleagues. Even so, what you lay down now becomes the ground you stand on for a long time.",
      "5": "Pleasure has to be earned in the year ahead, or so it feels. With Saturn in your fifth house, pleasure turns into a discipline, romance gets planned rather than left to chance, and you notice how rarely you play without a purpose. Creative work is slow but durable, and you finish what you start even on days when inspiration is thin. Romance runs cautious, with you holding back feelings until they seem safe to show. Children, your own or other people's, bring responsibility more than easy fun, and some days feel flat in a way that stings. The payoff is craft, the kind of skill that shows because you kept turning up.",
      "6": "Your daily routine becomes the main event of this year, with Saturn in the sixth house of your return chart. Workloads grow, deadlines tighten, and you become the person colleagues rely on to finish what others abandoned. Your body keeps score as well: the stiffness after long hours, the slump when you skip a meal, the tiredness no rest quite clears. You bring order to your meals, your exercise and your time with a precision that amuses your friends. The trap is overwork dressed up as virtue, taking on more because refusing feels like failure. By your next birthday your days run on sturdy systems rather than willpower, and you feel the difference.",
      "7": "Partnerships are tested and firmed up this year. With Saturn in the seventh house, you look hard at the bonds that matter most: a marriage, a business partner, the friend you lean on every week. Commitments get formalised through a wedding, a contract or a plain agreement about who does what, or one honest conversation ends something that has run its course. You spot the places where you give far more than you receive, and you stop pretending that is fine. Some months feel lonely even in company, and an older or more established person plays a large part in your story. Whatever survives these twelve months has weight, because you chose it with open eyes.",
      "8": "Shared money and deep trust come under scrutiny in the year ahead. Saturn in your eighth house can bring a loan, a tax bill, an estate to settle, or shared money that now needs proper rules. You read the small print and chase the forms everyone else lets slide. Emotionally, intimacy asks for patience: you feel exposed when you let someone see what you usually hide, so you guard your privacy more tightly than usual. Fear of loss sits close to the surface, sometimes around a death, a debt or an ending you did not choose. Facing these matters squarely is hard, yet it steadies you. By the end of this year you know what you owe and what is owed to you.",
      "9": "Beliefs meet real life this year, with Saturn in the ninth house of your return chart. You commit to learning something that truly counts, and progress is slower and harder won than you were led to expect. Journeys ask for more planning than spontaneity, and distant plans tend to arrive with a duty or obligation attached. Easy answers and slogans lose their appeal, including the ones you used to repeat yourself. Faith, spiritual or practical, feels drier than usual, and some weeks you wonder whether any of it holds. What survives the testing is a philosophy you have lived. You speak about what you believe with a quiet authority that others notice and respect.",
      "10": "Career takes centre stage in the year ahead. Saturn in your tenth house puts your work under a spotlight, and you are judged on results rather than promise. A senior role, a title with accountability, or overdue recognition for years of effort can all land in these twelve months. Weak spots show just as plainly: results that get questioned, and gaps in your skills that you can no longer ignore. Hours run long, and there are evenings when ambition feels more like duty than desire. Coasting is not an option this year, and you sense that from the first week. What you build now becomes part of your reputation long after this birthday has passed.",
      "11": "Friendships sort themselves out this year. With Saturn in the eleventh house of your return chart, you notice which circles drain you and which people turn up when it counts. Your circle shrinks a little and deepens, and you take on responsibility inside a team, a committee or a community project that leans on your reliability. Long range plans turn concrete: the five year savings target, the business you finally register. Some gatherings feel lonely, and you catch yourself on the edge of a crowd wondering why you came. The friends left standing at the end of these twelve months are the ones you trust with the serious things.",
      "12": "Much of the work this year happens behind closed doors. Saturn in your twelfth house pulls you inward, towards rest, reflection and the emotional business you usually stay busy enough to ignore. Tiredness surprises you, along with a pull towards solitude and old fears that return when everything is quiet. Caring for someone unwell, or a project done quietly and without credit, can fill the months. Progress feels invisible, and that frustrates the part of you that likes proof. Yet you are closing chapters and dropping habits that cost more than they give. The next cycle starts on cleared ground, and you feel lighter for it."
    },
    "uranus": {
      "1": "You surprise yourself in the year ahead. With Uranus in the first house of your return chart, the way you look and present yourself to the world changes, sometimes overnight. Routines that fitted perfectly last year start to chafe, and people who thought they knew you are caught off guard by the direction you take. There is electricity in your nervous system: ideas that strike without warning, a need to move, a short fuse when anyone tries to box you in. Rushing brings knocks, spills and near misses, so impatience carries a physical cost. What you gain is freedom to look and act like the person you have privately been becoming for years.",
      "2": "Income refuses to behave predictably this year. Uranus in your second house can bring a sudden windfall, a side project that takes off, or a bill that wipes out your buffer in a single week. The way you have always earned starts to bore you, and you find yourself researching freelancing, new platforms or a skill that pays in a different way. Impulse spending spikes on whatever feels new and exciting, and you know the feeling of checking your balance with one eye closed. Possessions that once reassured you begin to feel like clutter. A fresh route to financial independence opens up, and it works best when you keep a cushion for the months when money swings the other way.",
      "3": "Your mind runs faster than usual in the next twelve months. With Uranus in the third house of your return chart, ideas arrive in flashes, your attention jumps between interests, and conversations leap from topic to topic before anyone can keep up. A new subject or skill you never expected to care about suddenly absorbs you completely. Siblings, neighbours and your everyday surroundings throw up surprises, and news tends to reach you suddenly and out of nowhere. Your nerves feel wired, which shows in a racing mind and patchy sleep. Blunt words slip out before you have thought them through. By the close of the year you think in a different way.",
      "4": "Home is where the upheaval lands in the year ahead. Uranus in your fourth house can mean a sudden move, disruption at home, or a family change that rearranges who lives with you and how. Walls that once felt safe start to feel confining, and the urge to change your surroundings strikes on a whim. Relations with a parent can shift sharply, with honest words spoken that change the dynamic for good. Losing the sense of a fixed base unsettles you more than you admit to anyone. Underneath the disruption, a home life is forming that fits who you are now rather than who you were when you first set it up.",
      "5": "Romance and creativity turn electric this year. With Uranus in the fifth house of your return chart, attractions strike out of nowhere, often towards people who are nothing like your usual type, and flings flare and fade at speed. You create in bursts, pouring yourself into an idea for days and then leaving it untouched for weeks. Your interests change fast: you drop something you have loved for years and throw yourself into what nobody expected of you. Children, if you have them, startle you with their independence. Your hunger for freedom makes steady, predictable pleasures feel stale. The best moments of the year arrive unplanned, and saying yes to them leaves you more alive.",
      "6": "Daily routines refuse to hold still in the next twelve months. Uranus in your sixth house brings shake-ups at work: a new system, a restructure, a boss who leaves without notice, or your own leap into remote or freelance work. Repetitive tasks bore you so much that you start inventing shortcuts and automating whatever you can. Your body reacts fast to stress, with jittery energy, broken sleep and a nervous system that jumps at every interruption. Strict rules for your health and rigid schedules collapse within weeks. Flexible habits, reinvented as you go, are the ones that stick. By your next birthday the shape of your working day is almost unrecognisable from where it started.",
      "7": "Relationships go through sudden shifts in the year ahead. With Uranus in the seventh house of your return chart, someone new arrives out of the blue, a partner changes direction, or you realise you need far more space than a bond has been giving you. Unusual people are drawn to you and you to them, especially those from a completely different world who overturn your assumptions in a single conversation. Commitments feel tight, and you bristle when anyone tells you what a couple ought to do. Abrupt endings and quick beginnings both sit on the table. The partnerships that can hold your freedom become far more honest, and the rest fall away.",
      "8": "Shared resources and deep bonds bring surprises this year. Uranus in your eighth house can mean an unexpected inheritance, a partner's income changing overnight, a tax or insurance problem that appears from nowhere, or a debt cleared faster than planned. Intimacy feels charged and unpredictable, and you explore sides of desire that surprise you. Something breaks open psychologically as well: a secret comes out, or a fear you have carried for years loses its grip in a single moment. Keeping control is hard, and that unsettles you. Inside the shock sits liberation from old dependencies, financial or emotional, that stopped serving you some time ago.",
      "9": "Your worldview gets a jolt in the next twelve months. With Uranus in the ninth house of your return chart, a person or an idea arrives that rearranges what you believe. Travel plans change at short notice, and a journey you expected to take leads you somewhere else entirely. Learning takes an unconventional form, often self-directed, in a subject you had long ago written off. Dogma irritates you, and so do people who insist on one right answer. The hazard is leaping from belief to belief without ever settling on one. Your mind opens wider than it has in years, and you secretly enjoy the vertigo.",
      "10": "Career moves come fast and without warning this year. Uranus in your tenth house can bring a sudden promotion, a redundancy, a job offer you never applied for, or your own decision to walk out of a role that no longer fits. Rigid hierarchies grate on you, and the urge to work for yourself grows loud. Your public image changes too, often because you take a stand or something you say gets noticed by the right people. Stability is hard to find, which frightens the part of you that likes a clear ladder to climb. The career path emerging from all this looks far more like your own design than anyone else's.",
      "11": "Your social world gets reshuffled in the year ahead. With Uranus in the eleventh house of your return chart, new friends appear through unexpected channels and in places you would never have thought to look. Old friendships end abruptly or change shape after one frank conversation. Hopes for the future shift as well, and a goal you held for years feels irrelevant while a new one takes its place. Causes and people who think differently pull you in. Group plans fall through at short notice, and you learn not to rely on a single circle. What remains, as the year closes, is a crowd that feels like your real tribe.",
      "12": "Change works in the background this year. Uranus in your twelfth house stirs up vivid dreams, sudden insights that arrive out of nowhere, and flashes of memory you thought were long gone. Anxiety can rise without a clear cause, showing up as restless nights and a mind that refuses to switch off. Old self-sabotaging patterns break in odd moments, and you walk away from a habit you believed was permanent. Your inner life seeks unusual forms of stillness, and you follow spiritual impulses you would once have dismissed. Others see little of this, which leaves you feeling oddly out of step. Something that held you back for years lets go of you before your next birthday."
    },
    "neptune": {
      "1": "The way you come across softens and blurs in the year ahead. With Neptune in the first house of your return chart, people project onto you, seeing a healer, a muse or someone mysterious, and you find yourself playing along. Boundaries run thinner: you pick up the mood in a room before anyone speaks, and crowded places leave you drained. Your body is more sensitive too, reacting to stress and overload faster than usual. Direction goes hazy, and whole weeks drift by without a clear plan. Compassion and imagination are heightened, so beauty, creativity and quiet reflection feed you in a way they rarely do.",
      "2": "Money has a slippery quality this year. Neptune in your second house makes it easy to lose track of spending, trust a vague promise of payment, or lend generously and forget to follow up. Small leaks add up: a forgotten payment here, a loan to a friend there, money slipping away in ways you barely notice. Your values tilt towards meaning over gain, and creative, healing or charitable work becomes a steady source of income. Confusion or even deception around contracts and investments is a hazard, so a sharp eye on the paperwork protects you. Underneath it all you are rethinking what security means, and the answer turns out to be less about numbers than you expected.",
      "3": "Your thinking takes on a dreamy, intuitive colour in the next twelve months. With Neptune in the third house of your return chart, you daydream more, think in images and hear what people mean rather than what they say. Facts slip, though: you misread the time of a meeting, lose track of messages, or misremember a conversation entirely. Exchanges with siblings or neighbours turn foggy, with things left unsaid and misunderstandings that linger. Gossip and half truths travel around you. In their place, creative writing, music and imaginative learning flourish, and your intuition proves sharper than your logic on most days.",
      "4": "Home becomes a place of longing and mystery this year. Neptune in your fourth house blurs the facts around where you live: plans that keep slipping, problems that are hard to trace, a family secret that surfaces. You want your space to feel like a sanctuary, so softness, calm and beauty at home start to matter. Parents or relatives need your care, or disappoint you by not being who you hoped. Childhood memories drift up in quiet, ordinary moments. Feeling grounded is harder when your roots seem uncertain. Your home turns into a place of emotional rest rather than practical efficiency, and you guard that softness fiercely.",
      "5": "Romance turns cinematic in the year ahead. With Neptune in the fifth house of your return chart, you fall for potential rather than the person in front of you, filling the gaps with fantasy, and a crush feels like destiny within a week. Creativity flows wonderfully, and you create with the sense of being carried along. Pleasure slides into escapism easily, with one harmless indulgence quietly leading to the next. Children seem mysterious or need extra gentleness from you. Disappointment arrives whenever the dream meets the facts. Even so, this year hands you a kind of inspiration that few years offer.",
      "6": "Work and wellbeing become harder to pin down this year. Neptune in your sixth house brings a vague job description, a disorganised workplace, or colleagues whose promises dissolve on contact. Your energy rises and falls in ways you cannot explain, and your body reacts to stress and excess more than usual. Daily tasks without purpose drain you, while service, care work or creative jobs start to suit you. Boundaries slip whenever you keep saying yes to others and forget your own needs until you are running on empty. The days that go best in the next twelve months are gentle ones, with rest and quiet built in.",
      "7": "Partnerships carry a romantic glow and a hidden fog in the year ahead. With Neptune in the seventh house of your return chart, you see the best in a partner, sometimes more than is there, and forgive what you would question in anyone else. Someone can seem like a soulmate long before you truly know who they are. Rescuing, or being rescued, becomes a theme, with you playing therapist to the people you love. Confusion about commitment sits alongside the chance of a spiritual connection. Naming what you want from others is hard. By your next birthday a key relationship stands in much clearer light, whether that brings devotion or release.",
      "8": "Intimacy and shared money grow hazy this year. Neptune in your eighth house blurs joint finances, so a partner's debts or the details of a legacy stay frustratingly unclear, and tax or insurance paperwork hides mistakes. Emotionally you crave fusion, wanting to dissolve into another person completely. Sexual and spiritual experience overlap, and you feel things at a depth that words cannot quite reach. Dreams about people who have died carry an odd vividness. The danger lies in losing yourself, or being quietly manipulated by someone who knows your soft spots. Old fears around loss and control begin to soften over the months.",
      "9": "Your search for meaning intensifies in the next twelve months. With Neptune in the ninth house of your return chart, spiritual teachers, pilgrimages, retreats and faraway places that feel almost mythical draw you in. Mysticism fascinates you, and you believe more readily than usual. Travel plans go vague, with lost bookings and confusing connections, yet a single journey turns out to be one of the most magical of your life. Gurus, ideologies and ideas that sound too perfect can lead you astray. Art, religion, psychology or music feel natural to study. Your faith widens this year, along with your feeling for the invisible.",
      "10": "Your career direction gets misty in the year ahead. Neptune in your tenth house blurs professional goals, and you catch yourself in a role that has lost its clear shape or unsure what you are working towards. Colleagues project an idealised image onto you, or misread your intentions entirely. Rumours and muddled responsibilities cause friction, and you sometimes discover that the brief everyone agreed on meant something different to each person. At the same time a creative, healing or spiritual calling speaks to you loudly. Work that merely succeeds leaves you cold. Over these twelve months your public life moves closer to your ideals.",
      "11": "Friendships take on an idealistic tone this year. With Neptune in the eleventh house of your return chart, groups, causes and communities that promise something bigger than yourself pull you in. You befriend dreamers, artists and seekers, and your circle becomes a place of shared inspiration. Some friends prove less reliable than they seemed, and plans you hatch together drift off without anyone deciding to drop them. You give generously to the collective, sometimes at your own expense. Hopes for the future grow more compassionate and less concrete. The alliances that are real show themselves before this year is out.",
      "12": "Your inner world expands in the year ahead. Neptune in your twelfth house makes you sensitive to what is unseen: dreams feel prophetic, stillness comes easily, and you crave solitude and quiet. Other people's pain lands on you easily, and you need more rest than usual to stay balanced. Escapism tempts in whatever form is closest, and whole days can slip away in retreat. Compassion flows freely, and charity, care or creative work proves fulfilling. Old wounds dissolve gently when you stop guarding them. You end these twelve months more at peace with what lies beyond your control."
    },
    "pluto": {
      "1": "You come out of this year a different person. With Pluto in the first house of your return chart, something about your identity is stripped back to its core, and you feel it in your body, your appearance and the way you enter a room. People notice an intensity in you: the steady gaze, the fewer words, the decisions made quietly and absolutely. Power struggles flare when others try to steer you, and you do not back down. Sometimes the change is visible, in how you look, what you are willing to be called, or a role you stop playing. The process is uncomfortable and at times brutal. What emerges is a stronger, truer self that no longer needs anyone's approval.",
      "2": "Money and self-worth go through a deep overhaul in the year ahead. Pluto in your second house brings a dramatic change in income: a big rise, a painful loss, or a fight over what you are owed. You look hard at your possessions, letting go of what weighs you down and questioning what you really need. Control over money becomes emotional, and arguments about who pays for what cut deeper than the sums involved. Talents you undervalued turn out to earn more than you imagined. An obsession with security can grip you, so you check accounts compulsively. By the end of these twelve months your sense of worth rests on firmer, more honest ground.",
      "3": "Thinking and talking take on intensity this year. With Pluto in the third house of your return chart, conversations dig deep, you research topics obsessively, and you hear the hidden motives behind what people say. A sibling, neighbour or close contact brings a crisis or a revelation that changes how you see them. Your words carry force, and you feel the weight of everything you say before it leaves you. You fixate on a single idea or grievance, replaying an exchange for days. Psychology, research and investigation reward your attention. Your mind leaves the year sharper and far more penetrating.",
      "4": "Home and family go through deep change in the year ahead. Pluto in your fourth house brings a move, a renovation that exposes hidden problems, or a family crisis that shifts the balance of power between generations. Old childhood wounds resurface, sometimes through a parent's illness or a revelation about family history. You need control over your space, deciding who comes in and on what terms. The emotional intensity at home wears you out on some days. Still, the clearing goes deep, and you release what no longer protects you. Your emotional foundations are rebuilt from the ground up over these twelve months.",
      "5": "Love, pleasure and creativity turn intense this year. With Pluto in the fifth house of your return chart, a romance feels fated and consuming, with jealousy and passion never far apart. Creative work dives into dark or powerful themes, and you produce something that surprises even you. Children, yours or ones in your care, bring a turning point or a battle of wills. You pour yourself completely into whatever you enjoy, sometimes to the point of obsession, and nothing about fun stays light for long. Beneath the drama you discover how much power lives in your joy, and how much of yourself you had been holding back.",
      "6": "Your daily life and health go through a deep overhaul in the next twelve months. Pluto in your sixth house points to an all-consuming job, a toxic workplace you finally leave, or a role where you hold power over systems and people. Your body demands attention, and you change your diet, training or habits with total commitment. Stress settles in your gut and jaw, and you notice exactly what puts it there. Power struggles with colleagues or employers test your nerve. Perfectionism can tip into obsession, with you redoing tasks nobody else would notice. Your routines end the year leaner, healthier and far more your own.",
      "7": "Close relationships become the arena for transformation this year. With Pluto in the seventh house of your return chart, a partnership deepens intensely or ends dramatically, and you cannot keep it on the surface. You meet someone powerful who changes the course of your life, or you face control and jealousy inside an existing bond. Lawyers, contracts or a divorce can form part of the story. Your own shadow looks back at you from the people you are closest to, which is uncomfortable. Shallow connection stops being possible. The relationships still standing at the end of these twelve months are bound by trust that has been tested and held.",
      "8": "Deep change arrives through intimacy, shared money and loss in the year ahead. Pluto in your eighth house can bring an inheritance, a debt crisis, a merging of finances, or a death that rearranges your inner landscape. Sexuality and emotional closeness become intense, and you want nothing less than complete honesty from a partner. Secrets surface, yours or someone else's, and power games around money come into the open. Some weeks feel like standing on a cliff edge. Therapy, deep research and long honest conversations feel natural now. Something in you ends this year so that something stronger can grow in its place.",
      "9": "Your beliefs undergo a radical change in the next twelve months. With Pluto in the ninth house of your return chart, you question the ideas you grew up with, often after a crisis of faith or a conversation that shakes your certainty. Deep study pulls at you, particularly philosophies that deal with power, death and meaning. A journey abroad alters your perspective permanently, and you come home seeing your own town differently. Zeal is the hazard, and friends notice when you start preaching. Legal or academic matters turn into power struggles. The worldview you carry into next year is one you have fought for.",
      "10": "Career and public life go through deep transformation this year. Pluto in your tenth house brings power struggles with bosses, a rise to lasting influence, or the end of a career path altogether. A job that feels meaningless becomes intolerable, and you want authority that matches your ability. Your reputation is highly visible, and the scrutiny can feel invasive. Relationships with authority figures, including a parent, come under pressure. You learn how to hold power without abusing it or giving it away too cheaply. Your professional identity gets rebuilt on stronger foundations over the year ahead, with little of the old version left.",
      "11": "Friendships and group life go through deep change this year. With Pluto in the eleventh house of your return chart, some friendships end abruptly, while others deepen into bonds that feel fated. You get involved with groups where power matters, and you see who pulls the strings in every one of them. Long term goals transform, often after the realisation that an old dream no longer means anything to you. A collective cause grips you and takes up your evenings. Manipulation or jealousy in a social circle hurts more than you let on. The next twelve months leave you with fewer allies, and far truer ones.",
      "12": "Deep inner work defines the year ahead. Pluto in your twelfth house brings buried feelings, fears and memories to the surface, often through dreams or long stretches of solitude. You feel pulled towards therapy, spiritual practice or long, undisturbed hours of reflection. Hidden opponents or secret matters come to light, sometimes at work, sometimes in the family. Nights of anxiety or grief arrive without an obvious trigger. You meet the parts of yourself you usually avoid, and you stay with them longer than before. A heavy, invisible weight lifts from you before your next birthday, and you feel the space it leaves."
    }
  },
  "sign": {
    "mercury": {
      "aries": "Mercury in Aries in your return chart speeds up your mind for the year. You answer before the question is finished, and you say out loud what everyone else was still working out how to put. Decisions come quickly and usually from the gut, which saves you weeks of dithering over plans you already knew the answer to. Your words land harder than you intend, though, and a blunt remark made in the heat of the moment can take weeks to repair. Arguments flare and burn out fast, and you are often the first to forget them. This is a year for pitching, starting things, speaking up first and learning by doing rather than waiting until you feel ready.",
      "taurus": "With Mercury in Taurus in your return chart, your thinking slows down and gets sturdier. You would rather understand one thing properly than skim ten, and you learn best through practical, hands-on experience that proves itself in real life. Once you have made up your mind, you hold the view with calm stubbornness, and people notice that you are hard to rush or talk round. Conversations about money, property and value come up often, and you handle them well. The drawback is a closed door: you hear a new idea, decide it is nonsense and stop listening halfway through. Your words carry weight this year precisely because you say them slowly and mean them.",
      "gemini": "Your mind runs on several tracks at once this year, with Mercury in Gemini in the return chart. You follow several conversations, interests and plans at once, and somehow you keep up with all of it. Curiosity pulls you in every direction at once, and chance conversations with near strangers turn into useful contacts. Messages, short trips and paperwork multiply, and you are good at all three. Scattering is the real cost: things left half finished, replies never sent, plans that change again and again. When you pick one thread and follow it to the end, this year's quick wit turns into something you can show people.",
      "cancer": "Mercury in Cancer in your return chart makes this a year when you think with your feelings. You remember how someone said something long after the words themselves have faded, and a flat tone can colour your whole day. Conversations about family, home and the past take up more of your time, and the full story behind something from your early life finally comes out. Your memory is excellent and your listening tender, so people bring you their worries. Taking remarks personally is the cost, and you replay a small comment over and over until it hardens into a grievance. Putting your feelings into words, even privately and just for yourself, brings unusual clarity this year.",
      "leo": "This year you speak as if you have an audience, and quite often you do. With Mercury in Leo in your return chart, your stories get bigger, your delivery warmer and your opinions more confidently stated. You are the one people turn to when something needs saying well, and your words get repeated long after you have said them. Creative writing, teaching and any work where your voice is the product go well. Pride gets in the way when someone questions your idea in front of others, and you dig in rather than admit the flaw you privately spotted. Speaking from the heart rather than performing is what makes people remember your words long after the year is out.",
      "virgo": "Mercury in Virgo in your return chart sharpens your eye for detail. You spot the wrong detail, the figure that does not add up and the missing step everyone else overlooked without a second thought. Lists, systems and routines appeal strongly, and you finally sort out the parts of your life you have been meaning to fix for years. Work that needs precision and analysis suits you well for the next twelve months. Your inner critic is loud, though, and you go over simple things again and again or dwell on one mistake in an otherwise good week. The most useful thing you produce this year is practical, careful and helpful to someone else.",
      "libra": "Your conversations this year revolve around balance and fairness, because Mercury sits in Libra in your return chart. You see both sides of every disagreement so clearly that friends ask you to mediate, and you are good at it. Your tone softens and your wording turns diplomatic, which smooths negotiations, contracts and difficult family chats. Partnerships of every kind involve a lot of talking, and much gets agreed in pairs rather than alone. Indecision is the snag: you weigh two options for so long that the choice gets made for you, or you agree to keep the peace and resent it later. Saying what you think, kindly, is where this year's measurable progress lies.",
      "scorpio": "Mercury in Scorpio in your return chart gives you a detective's mind for the year. Small talk bores you; you want to know what is going on, and you read the silences in a conversation better than the words. Research, investigation, therapy and matters involving other people's money all suit your focus now. Secrets come your way, sometimes because people trust you and sometimes because you went looking. Suspicion is the dark edge, and you can build a whole theory from one ambiguous word or silence. You keep your own counsel more than usual, and the few things you finally say out loud land with force.",
      "sagittarius": "Big ideas take over your thinking this year, with Mercury in Sagittarius in your return chart. You want the overview, not the small print, and you get excited about big plans, philosophy and ideas that rearrange how you see the world. You speak frankly and with enthusiasm, and your honesty often makes people laugh. The small print still matters, though, and you miss a deadline, overpromise or tell a friend a truth they were not ready to hear. Arguments about beliefs, politics or religion come up more than usual, and you rarely hold back. Teaching, publishing and long conversations with people from different backgrounds are where your mind opens widest.",
      "capricorn": "Mercury in Capricorn in your return chart makes your thinking practical and strategic for the year. You plan in quarters rather than days, and you want every conversation to lead somewhere concrete. Contracts, career plans, formal letters and serious negotiations go well because you sound credible and prepared. You speak less than usual, yet people listen closely when you do. Pessimism creeps in when you are tired, and you talk yourself out of a good idea by listing every way it could fail. A dry, well-timed joke is your best tool in a tense room. What you learn this year, often the hard way, becomes lasting expertise that people start paying for.",
      "aquarius": "Your thinking this year runs ahead of the room, since Mercury sits in Aquarius in your return chart. You have ideas nobody else has had yet, and you are happy to voice them even when the group goes quiet. Technology, science, new ideas and social causes pull your attention, and you find your people in the most unexpected places. You argue from principle and stay remarkably detached when others are upset, which helps in a crisis and chills things when people want warmth. Stubborn contrarianism is the weak spot: you disagree partly because everyone else agrees. The unusual idea you keep returning to this year deserves to be taken seriously.",
      "pisces": "Mercury in Pisces in your return chart makes your mind porous and imaginative this year. You pick up the mood in a room before anyone speaks, and you understand people through images, music and feeling rather than tidy logic. Imagination and spiritual ideas flow easily, and your dreams are vivid enough to stay with you well into the day. Practical communication suffers: details slip through your fingers, and a vague reply leads to a misunderstanding you then have to untangle. You also absorb other people's worries as if they were your own. Trusting your intuition while still checking the facts turns this year's thinking into something gently wise."
    },
    "venus": {
      "aries": "Venus in Aries in your return chart makes love bold and immediate this year. You know within minutes whether you are attracted to someone, and you usually act on it, making the first move yourself. In an existing relationship you want more spark, adventure and honesty, and you would rather pick a fight than settle for anything lukewarm. Spending is impulsive too, driven by whatever you want right now and cannot bear to wait for. Boredom arrives quickly once the chase is over, and that is the real test for any bond this year. Passion kept alive with shared challenges, rather than new faces, is what warms the year.",
      "taurus": "Slow, sensual and reliable is how love wants to be, with Venus in Taurus in your return chart. You show affection through touch, steady care and small comforts chosen with love, and you want the same in return. Existing relationships deepen through routine pleasures and the quiet comfort of familiar rituals you share. Money flows more steadily, and you get deep satisfaction from buying one beautiful, lasting thing rather than ten cheap ones. Possessiveness surfaces, and you cling to a person or a habit long after it has stopped feeding you. Comfort, beauty and loyalty are what you build here, and they outlast the year.",
      "gemini": "Venus in Gemini in your return chart makes conversation the heart of your love life this year. Flirting happens through words, a clever reply sets your pulse going, and you fall for a mind before a face. Variety matters: new people, new experiences, and a partner who can keep up with your changing moods. Spending scatters across many small pleasures and passing interests rather than one big purchase. Commitment wobbles when a relationship goes quiet, and someone new tempts you because they are new and have fresh things to say. Keeping the talk lively with the person you already love keeps the whole year sparkling.",
      "cancer": "Love turns towards home and safety this year, because Venus sits in Cancer in your return chart. You want to be looked after and to look after someone, and you show it through small, constant acts of care that make home feel like a nest. Family ties soften, and you enjoy nurturing people and gathering the ones you love close. Spending goes on comfort and security, on anything that makes your home feel safer, softer and more yours. Hurt feelings go underground, and you sulk or withdraw rather than say you felt neglected. Letting yourself be cared for as generously as you care for others makes this year's relationships nourishing.",
      "leo": "Venus in Leo in your return chart puts romance, glamour and generosity at the centre of your year. You want to be adored, and you are happy to adore in return with grand gestures, generous surprises and loud public affection. Anything that lets you shine, play and express yourself brings joy, and people notice you more than usual. Spending leans towards the lavish, both on yourself and on the people you want to spoil. Wounded pride is the flashpoint: a partner who forgets to praise you can feel like a partner who has stopped caring. Love that is playful and openly celebrated, rather than tested, is what lights you up.",
      "virgo": "Small, practical acts carry your love this year, with Venus in Virgo in your return chart. You take care of the practical things for the people you love and notice they are low before they say a word. Affection feels real to you when it is useful and consistent, not when it is showy. Money gets careful attention, and you enjoy budgeting, hunting down the better deal and spending on health and quality everyday things. Criticism slips in where tenderness belongs, and you point out what went wrong when you meant to say you missed them. Steady care with a little less correction is what lets your relationships flourish.",
      "libra": "Venus in Libra in your return chart makes partnership the theme of your year. You want harmony, beauty and fairness, and your charm is at full strength, smoothing tensions at work and at home. Relationships begin, deepen or become official, and you care about how the two of you look together. Art, music, good design and pleasant surroundings lift your mood more than usual, and a fair share of your money goes on them. People-pleasing is the price: you say yes to plans and people you do not want, then feel quietly resentful afterwards. Choosing honesty over surface peace is what turns this year's relationships into a meeting of equals.",
      "scorpio": "Love runs deep and intense this year with Venus in Scorpio in your return chart. Casual does not interest you; you want total honesty, loyalty and a bond that reaches the parts of you most people never see. Attraction feels magnetic and a little obsessive, and you think about one person far more than you admit. Shared money, debts and inheritances come into focus, and anything you hold with someone else calls for clear agreements. Jealousy and control flare when you feel insecure, and you test a partner in quiet ways rather than ask for reassurance. Relationships that survive your full intensity come out stronger by your next birthday, and those that cannot end decisively.",
      "sagittarius": "Venus in Sagittarius in your return chart wants love to feel like an adventure this year. You are drawn to people from different backgrounds and to a partner who makes you laugh and can talk about big ideas for hours. Travel, learning and freedom feel romantic now, and a shared adventure does more for a relationship than any comfortable routine. Money goes on experiences and discoveries far more than on things. Restlessness is the danger, and you feel hemmed in by ordinary obligations and blame the person rather than the routine. Keeping space and a shared horizon in view lets your relationships grow rather than shrink.",
      "capricorn": "Love gets serious this year, with Venus in Capricorn in your return chart. You want commitment, respect and a partner who turns up when it counts, and flattery or drama leaves you cold. Relationships that have lasted are tested and often formalised, while newer ones move slowly and deliberately. Money is handled with discipline, and you spend on quality that holds its value or invest in your own future. Emotional reserve is the cost: you show affection by working hard for someone and forget to say it. Warmth that people can see, and not only rely on, is what makes your bonds this year sturdy and lasting.",
      "aquarius": "Venus in Aquarius in your return chart gives your love life an unconventional streak this year. Friendship is the foundation of every bond you value, and you are drawn to people who are different, independent and a little unusual. You need room to breathe, and a partner who respects your space earns more affection than one who hovers. Groups, online communities and causes bring new connections, some of them surprising. Money goes on technology, social projects or sudden changes of taste. Detachment is the snag, and you go cool and analytical just when someone needs you close. Letting love be both free and warm makes this year's relationships feel your own.",
      "pisces": "Love this year is tender, romantic and a little dreamy, with Venus in Pisces in your return chart. You feel what your partner feels, forgive easily and are moved to tears by beauty and small kindnesses. Compassion comes without effort, and you give time and money to people who need help. Creative and spiritual pursuits bring deep pleasure. Idealisation is the hazard: you see someone as they could be rather than as they are, or you rescue a person who does not want saving. Spending blurs too, with money slipping away on treats and good causes. Keeping one foot on the ground lets this year's love be as beautiful as you imagine it."
    },
    "mars": {
      "aries": "Mars in Aries in your return chart gives you a year of raw energy and bold starts. You want to move, compete and win, and you take on the challenge that everyone said was too much. Your body wants physical outlets, and hard effort clears your head faster than any conversation. Anger flares quickly and burns out just as fast, but it leaves damage when you snap at people who did nothing wrong. Minor cuts, bumps and burns come from rushing, usually on your most impatient days. Courage is this year's great asset, and it opens doors that caution never would.",
      "taurus": "Steady, slow and stubborn: that is your energy for the year, with Mars in Taurus in your return chart. You work patiently towards something tangible, a result you can see and hold once the effort is done. Once you commit, nothing moves you, and people learn that pushing you only makes you dig in. Your stamina is excellent, and you outlast colleagues who started faster and louder. Anger takes a long time to build and a long time to leave, and a grievance about money or possessions can simmer for months. Pointing that determination at something worth owning gives you results that are solid and lasting.",
      "gemini": "Mars in Gemini in your return chart puts your energy into words, ideas and constant movement this year. You juggle several projects, write, talk and connect with people at speed, always with something else on the go. Arguments are verbal, quick and clever, and you win debates with a sharp comeback, sometimes one you regret by the evening. Nervous energy needs outlets, and movement, variety and learning new skills all help. Scattering is the weak point, with too many tasks started and too few finished, and a restless mind that makes sleep patchy. Directing your wit at one clear goal turns this year's mental energy into achievement.",
      "cancer": "Your drive runs through your feelings this year, since Mars sits in Cancer in your return chart. You fight fiercely for family and home, and you put energy into renovating, moving or protecting the people you love. Anger rarely comes out directly; you go quiet, turn cool or make a pointed remark instead of saying you are hurt. Moods govern your energy strongly, and a bad morning at home drains you at work. Old family patterns stir up conflict, particularly around who does what. When you let yourself be honestly angry and then move on, this year's protective strength becomes an asset.",
      "leo": "Mars in Leo in your return chart makes your year bold, creative and proud. You want to lead, perform and be recognised, and you pour energy into projects that carry your name and anything that lets you shine. Confidence runs high, and you step into the spotlight without a moment's hesitation. Your generosity is energetic too, and you bring a warmth to every gathering that people talk about afterwards. Clashes come when your pride is wounded, and you escalate a small slight into a scene. Putting your fire into something you love rather than into being right brings creative wins.",
      "virgo": "Doing things properly is where your energy goes, with Mars in Virgo in your return chart. You tackle the clutter, the health routine and the work backlog with methodical focus, and a finished task done well gives you deep satisfaction. Colleagues rely on your efficiency and your eye for detail. Fitness improves through regular, sensible habits rather than heroic bursts. Irritation shows up as nitpicking, and you criticise the way others handle tasks you would have done differently. Overwork is the real danger, with stress landing in your stomach or your sleep. Practical service, given without martyrdom, is where this year's effort pays off.",
      "libra": "Mars in Libra in your return chart makes your year about acting with and through other people. You get more done in partnership, and joint ventures, collaborations and relationship decisions take up much of your energy. You fight for fairness, often on someone else's behalf, and you are persuasive when you argue a just cause. Your own anger is harder to express, and you swallow irritation to keep the peace until it leaks out sideways as sarcasm or quiet resistance. Indecision slows you when two options look equally reasonable. Saying plainly what you want, while staying fair, is where your momentum comes from.",
      "scorpio": "This year your drive is intense, focused and private, with Mars in Scorpio in your return chart. When you want something you pursue it with total concentration, quietly and without announcing your plans. Research, financial strategy, therapy and any work that means digging beneath the surface go very well. Power struggles come up, sometimes over shared money or control, and you do not back down. Anger runs cold rather than hot, and you hold grudges longer than is good for you. Channelled well, your resolve transforms a situation completely; left to fester, it poisons it. Whatever you commit to, you reach through sheer will.",
      "sagittarius": "Mars in Sagittarius in your return chart fills your year with restless, adventurous energy. You want to travel, study, explore and push your limits, and anything that widens your horizons recharges you like nothing else. You fight passionately for your beliefs and argue about principles with conviction. Enthusiasm makes you take on more than you can manage, so you overcommit, overpromise or start something big and drop it halfway. Your tongue turns sharp when you feel preached at, even though you preach yourself. Aimed at a big, meaningful goal, this energy carries you a remarkably long way.",
      "capricorn": "Your energy this year is disciplined and ambitious, with Mars in Capricorn in your return chart. You set a clear goal, often in your career, and work towards it steadily, putting in the effort others avoid. People in authority notice your competence, and your responsibilities grow. You stay controlled in conflict, which gives you an advantage, but you also bottle up frustration until it comes out as coldness. Joints, teeth and back feel the strain of pushing hard without rest. Patient effort brings real, measurable results, the kind you can point to when the year turns.",
      "aquarius": "Mars in Aquarius in your return chart puts your energy into change, independence and causes you believe in. You want to do things your own way, and you rebel against rules that make no sense to you. Group projects, campaigns, technology and innovation all attract your drive. You fight for the collective and can be startlingly brave when defending someone else's rights. Conflicts are cool and intellectual, but you turn stubbornly contrary, refusing to budge just to prove a point. Sudden bursts of energy alternate with spells of detachment. The inventive work you start this year is often ahead of its time.",
      "pisces": "This year your drive is gentle, intuitive and hard to pin down, with Mars in Pisces in your return chart. You act on hunches and feelings, and you get more done when you are inspired than when you force it. Creative, spiritual and caring work absorbs your energy beautifully. Confrontation feels exhausting, so you drift away from conflict, agree to things you do not want or let resentment leak out indirectly. Your energy fluctuates, and you need more rest than usual. Fighting for someone vulnerable brings out surprising strength. Trusting your instincts while setting clear limits makes this a quietly powerful year."
    }
  },
  "retro": {
    "mercury": "Mercury retrograde in your return chart turns your mind inward this year. You rethink rather than start fresh, returning to old projects, unfinished writing, shelved plans and people you lost touch with. Messages go astray, travel plans shift and technology glitches more than usual, so you learn to check the details twice. Your inner voice becomes loud and reflective, and you understand things by going over them again, often in quiet moments alone. Conversations you left unfinished come back for another round. Second thoughts serve you better than first ones. By the year's end, whatever you have revised is sharper than anything you would have rushed.",
    "venus": "Venus retrograde in this year's return chart sends you back over your relationships and values. An old flame resurfaces, a former friend gets in touch, or you look at your current partnership with new and sometimes uncomfortable clarity. What once attracted you no longer pulls in the same way, and your taste in clothes, art or people shifts. Impulse purchases this year often turn into regrets, so spending needs a pause. Self-worth comes up for review, and you notice where you have settled for less than you deserve. Love that survives this honest reassessment becomes more genuine. Slowly, and for good, you come to value yourself on your own terms.",
    "mars": "Mars retrograde in your return chart turns your energy inward this year. Projects start more slowly, and frustration builds when things do not move as fast as you want. Anger is harder to express directly, so you replay old arguments or feel an irritation you cannot quite place. Revisiting unfinished goals rewards you far more than launching new ones, and a plan you abandoned years ago comes back with fresh purpose. Your body asks for smarter effort and better recovery rather than pushing harder. Strategy beats force. Twelve months on, you act from inner conviction rather than outside pressure.",
    "jupiter": "Jupiter retrograde in your return chart makes growth an inner journey this year. Luck and opportunity arrive less through outward expansion and more through reflection, study and a shift in belief. You reconsider the philosophy, faith or grand plan you once held, and you find new meaning in ideas you had dismissed. Travel works best when it takes you back to places you know or people from your past. Overconfidence is corrected without fuss, and you notice where you promised too much. Generosity turns towards yourself as well as others, which feels unfamiliar at first. The wisdom you gain is personal, hard won and enduring.",
    "saturn": "Saturn retrograde in your return chart asks you to rebuild your inner structure this year. Responsibilities you carried out of duty come under question, and you decide which commitments belong to you. Old fears, family expectations or a harsh inner critic surface for review, often in the quiet hours when you are alone with your thoughts. Progress in your career or long-term plans feels slower. You become your own authority, setting your own standards instead of waiting for approval. Discipline turns into self-respect rather than self-punishment. By the end of these twelve months you are steadier, clearer and more in charge of your life.",
    "uranus": "Uranus spends around five months of every year retrograde, so here it colours your personal year rather than marking anything rare. Your urge for freedom works more internally, and changes brew quietly for months before anyone else sees them. Old restlessness returns, a rebellion you set aside or a dream of a very different life, and you reconsider what independence means to you. Sudden events feel less like shocks from outside and more like awakenings from within. Old habits break slowly rather than all at once, which makes the change stick. In the end you know which changes are yours alone and which were a reaction.",
    "neptune": "Neptune spends nearly half of each year retrograde, so its turn here speaks to how your year feels inside rather than to a rare event. Your imagination, spirituality and dreams turn inward, and you look for meaning privately, through stillness, reflection and time alone. Illusions you held about a person, a job or yourself gently dissolve, which feels disappointing before it feels freeing. Intuition deepens, and you notice patterns and coincidences more. Escapism tempts you when life feels heavy, so this year teaches you what restores you and what only numbs you. Gradually you come to trust your inner compass more than outside approval.",
    "pluto": "Pluto is retrograde for around five months each year, and in your return chart it points your transformation inward. Power struggles play out inside you more than with other people, and you confront old fears, compulsions or buried memories. Something you have held onto too long is ready to go, even though letting it go feels uncomfortable. You examine where you give your power away and where you grip too tightly. Therapy, research and unflinching self-examination bring profound results. When the year closes you feel renewed, with a strength that came from facing what you had avoided.",
    "chiron": "Chiron retrograde in your return chart turns this year's healing inward. Old wounds, particularly those around belonging, worth or feeling different, resurface for gentle attention. You understand your own pain more clearly instead of rushing to fix everyone else's. Past experiences come back in memory or through events that echo them, and this time you respond with more wisdom than you had before. Your sensitivity to other people's suffering runs high, and you learn to care for yourself first. Therapy, bodywork and honest conversations are especially healing now. Year's end finds the scar turned into a source of strength and quiet authority.",
    "northNode": "The lunar nodes move backwards almost all of the time, so a retrograde North Node in your return chart is its natural motion. This year your direction of growth unfolds through reflection as much as action, and you recognise lessons that echo earlier chapters of your life. Meetings that feel fated, or situations that feel strangely familiar, point you towards your path. You make progress by trusting the unfamiliar pull even when the old pattern feels safer. By your next birthday you are noticeably closer to the person you are becoming."
  }
};
window.AstroDeep.oobRich = {
  "moon": "With the Moon out of bounds in your birth chart, your emotional life runs wider and deeper than most people's. You feel things at full volume: the slightest moment can move you to tears, and your moods shift faster than the people around you can follow. Many people with this placement learned early to look after themselves emotionally, because the adults nearby did not quite understand what they needed. Your intuition is often startlingly accurate, and you sense the atmosphere of a room before anyone speaks. Being told how to feel makes you bristle, because emotional freedom matters to you. Others find you hard to predict, yet your inner world is rich, original and fiercely your own.",
  "mercury": "Mercury out of bounds in your birth chart gives you a mind that works outside the usual lines. You make connections others miss, jump to conclusions that turn out to be right and find ordinary explanations dull. School often felt ill-fitting, as though the teaching was designed for a different kind of brain, and you learned more from your own reading and curiosity. Your speech and writing have an unusual voice, and people remember the way you put things. You also lose people when you leap ahead without showing your working. Your gift is original thought, the kind that invents, writes and sees around corners.",
  "venus": "With Venus out of bounds in your birth chart, you love and value on your own terms. Your taste is distinctive, often ahead of fashion, and you are drawn to beauty that others overlook or find odd. Ordinary rules about relationships never quite fitted you, and you have felt out of step with how others date, commit or show affection. You bring striking artistic talent, and your eye for beauty shows in everything you touch. The difficulty is feeling misunderstood in love, or squeezing yourself into a template that was never yours. Trusting your own idea of beauty and connection turns it into something others learn from.",
  "mars": "Mars out of bounds in your birth chart gives you a drive that follows no template. Your energy comes in intense bursts, and when something matters you act with a boldness others find startling. You take risks people around you would not, and you fight for things in your own way, often alone. Rules about how to compete, argue or assert yourself never felt natural, and you work best where you set the pace. Your temper and your stamina both surprise people, including you. Restraint is hard to learn, and burnout follows the big push. Channelled well, this is pioneering courage that breaks new ground.",
  "jupiter": "With Jupiter out of bounds in your birth chart, your appetite for meaning and growth reaches beyond the familiar. You are drawn to unusual beliefs, unconventional teachers, distant places and ideas your family never considered. Your generosity is large, sometimes extravagant, and you give time, money or encouragement without calculating the return. Luck reaches you through odd routes, arriving by paths nobody else would think to take. Excess is the flip side, whether overpromising, overindulging or throwing yourself too wholeheartedly into a new cause. Your faith in possibility is contagious, and it helps the people around you dare to hope bigger.",
  "saturn": "Saturn out of bounds in your birth chart means you build your own rules. The traditional routes to authority, whether school, the career ladder or family expectation, rarely fitted you, and you sensed early that the usual structures were not made for you. So you create the framework you could not find, often in your own business, discipline or way of living. Your sense of responsibility is strong but unconventional, and you hold yourself to standards others cannot see. Lessons arrive in unusual forms and take longer to land, yet what you learn lasts. The authority you earn is entirely self-made and respected.",
  "uranus": "Uranus out of bounds in your birth chart is rare, and it doubles your independent streak. You feel most alive when you are breaking new ground, and conventional life has always felt like a costume that does not fit. Sudden changes, unusual interests and leaps of insight run through your story. People find you unpredictable, and you find routine suffocating. Your originality made you feel like an outsider, particularly when you were young and everyone else seemed to know the rules. That same originality makes you an inventor, reformer or awakener in whatever field you choose, and your ideas often arrive before the world is ready for them.",
  "neptune": "With Neptune out of bounds in your birth chart, a rare placement, your imagination and sensitivity reach well beyond the usual range. You pick up atmospheres, moods and unspoken feelings with uncanny accuracy, and you absorb other people's emotions as if they were your own. Music, art, spirituality and dreams speak to you with unusual power, and a single moving experience can stay with you for weeks. Boundaries are hard, and you lose yourself in a person, a cause or an escape. Practical life needs extra structure to keep you grounded. At full strength, this placement gives visionary creativity and a compassion that feels boundless.",
  "pluto": "Pluto out of bounds in your birth chart is uncommon and shared by your generation, marking a time when collective power and transformation broke familiar limits. For you personally, it colours how intensely you feel themes of control, change and survival. You sense the hidden currents in families, workplaces and whole societies, and surface appearances rarely fool you. Crises transform you rather than defeat you, and people notice how you come back from them. You also feel the pull towards extremes, all or nothing, with little patience for half measures. Your capacity for regeneration is remarkable, and you help others find strength in what they had thought was the end."
};
